      {
        "n": "SEA TO SEA W/ DIANA RATSAMEE",
        "s": "2026-10-28T20:00:00Z",
        "e": "2026-10-28T21:00:00Z",
        "d": "Seattle DJ and collector Diana Ratsamee digs out musical discoveries from across the world, notably sharing music from Lao and Thailand and Southeast Asia - airing rock, disco, soul and psychedelic records, as well as diving into present day musical movements in the region.\nFrom the host: \"Today’s show is about immigrant solidarity. As the child of Lao refugees, I’ve always felt a deep connection to our immigrant neighbors in Latin America. As our communities face increasing attacks from the current administration, solidarity feels more important than ever.\"",
        "j": null,
        "u": "https://www.nts.live/api/v2/shows/diana-ratsamee/episodes/diana-ratsamee-28th-october-2026"
      },
      {
        "n": "Ela Minus - Ekleido's Femina Score",
        "s": "2026-10-28T21:00:00Z",
        "e": "2026-10-28T22:00:00Z",
        "d": "Colombia-born, NYC based artist Ela Minus continues her NTS residency.\nFrom the host: \"The original score by Floating Points, Stella Mozgawa and me -Ela Minus- for Femina. The highly anticipated new work from award-winning choreographic duo Ekleido (Hannah Ekholm and Faye Stoeser); Femina questions how femininity is perceived, embodied and valued through time. London Premiere Nov 5 -7\"",
